data: {"text":"1. That the applicant apprehends arrest in connection with FIR No. 215/2026 dated 10.04.2026 registered at PS Gandhi Maidan under Sections 318(4)"}

data: {"text":" and 336(3) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023. The applicant has not been arrested so far but"}

data: {"text":" reasonably apprehends arrest in the said case and hence seeks anticipatory bail from"}

data: {"text":" this Hon'ble Court.\n\n2. That the applicant apprehends arrest in connection with FIR No. 215/2026 dated 10.04.2"}

data: {"text":"026 lodged at PS Gandhi Maidan, Patna. The said FIR has been lodged on the basis of a false and malicious complaint by the de-facto complainant arising out of a purely civil business"}

data: {"text":" dispute between the parties.\n\n3. That the applicant is a businessman of standing in the community and has been conducting his"}

data: {"text":" business activities in a lawful manner. The present case is nothing but an attempt by"}

data: {"text":" the complainant to misuse the criminal law machinery to settle personal"}

data: {"text":" scores arising out of commercial transactions between the parties.\n\n4. That the applicant has deep roots in the community and has no"}

data: {"text":" criminal antecedents whatsoever. He is a law-abiding citizen who has never been involved in any criminal activity and undertakes to cooperate fully with the investigation."}

data: {"text":" The applicant further undertakes not to leave the territorial jurisdiction of the State of Bihar without prior permission of this Hon'ble Court.\n\n5. That the allegations"}

data: {"text":" made against the applicant are completely false and fabricated. The applicant has been falsely implicated in the present case due"}

data: {"text":" to the malicious intent of the complainant who wants to pressurize the applicant in connection"}

data: {"text":" with their business dealings.\n\n6. That the dispute between the applicant and the complainant is purely civil in nature pertaining to business transactions and commercial"}

data: {"text":" dealings. The complainant has deliberately given a criminal colour to the civil"}

data: {"text":" dispute to harass and intimidate the applicant.\n\n7. That the applicant being a person of clean ant"}

data: {"text":"ecedents with no previous criminal record and having deep roots in the society, there is no likelihood"}

data: {"text":" of his fleeing from justice or tampering with evidence. The applicant is ready"}

data: {"text":" and willing to join the investigation as and when called upon by the investigating agency.\n\n8. That cust"}

data: {"text":"odial interrogation of the applicant is not at all necessary as the applicant is willing to cooperate with the investigation and join the same whenever"}

data: {"text":" required. The applicant undertakes to appear before the investigating officer as and when summoned and shall not hamper the investigation in any manner"}

data: {"text":".\n\n9. That the fundamental right to life and liberty guaranteed under Article 21 of the Constitution of India includes the right to be free from arbitrary arrest."}

data: {"text":" The Hon'ble Supreme Court in Sushila Aggarwal v. State (2020) 5 SCC 1 has laid down the conditions"}

data: {"text":" for granting anticipatory bail, including consideration of the nature and gravity of accusation, antecedents"}

data: {"text":" of the applicant, and possibility of fleeing from justice.\n\n10. That the present case does not involve any grave"}

data: {"text":" or serious offence and the allegations are bailable in nature. The applicant has strong roots"}

data: {"text":" in the community and there is no possibility of his absconding or fleeing from justice. Grant of anticipatory bail would"}

data: {"text":" not prejudice the investigation in any manner.\n\n11. That the applicant is ready"}

data: {"text":" and willing to abide by any conditions that this Hon'ble Court may deem fit to impose while"}

data: {"text":" granting anticipatory bail. The applicant undertakes to make himself available for interrogation as and when required by the investigating agency and shall not directly"}

data: {"text":" or indirectly contact any witness in the case.\n\n12. That in the interest of justice and considering the facts and circumstances of the case, the"}

data: {"text":" applicant deserves to be enlarged on anticipatory bail. The continued threat of"}

data: {"text":" arrest is causing immense mental agony and harassment to the applicant and is"}

data: {"text":" affecting his fundamental right to life and liberty."}

